seg-edcaed830e15 = The trade reads both ways. At equal C/N₀, ranging accuracy is set by the chip rate and the band (wide C ranges five times finer than L). At equal radiated power the free-space loss charges the higher bands in full: C band loses { "12.5" } dB of C/N₀ and ranges four times worse than L, UHF gains { "8.2" } dB, while carrying { "6.6" } times the ionospheric delay. Wide C buys its accuracy back with bandwidth. These rest on the representative designs and on isotropic antennas; a directional user antenna at C band changes the equal-EIRP columns.

